  <h2>Build one subject clause and one zero object clause</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the trainer who teaches evenings is available" data-hint="Begin with the trainer; keep who because it is the subject of teaches, then complete the main clause with is available." data-fix="The trainer who teaches evenings is available." data-success-message="Correct. Who supplies the subject of teaches, and the complete noun phrase controls is available.">
    <h3>Build 1: keep the subject relative</h3><p class="tile-target">Identify the available trainer by that person’s teaching schedule.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="available">available</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="trainer">trainer</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="evenings">evenings</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="who">who</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="teaches">teaches</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the projector Omar tested is in Room Three" data-hint="Begin with the projector, follow it directly with clause subject Omar and verb tested, then finish the main clause. The object relative word is intentionally omitted." data-fix="The projector Omar tested is in Room Three." data-success-message="Correct. Omar remains the subject of tested, and the projector is its understood object without a repeated pronoun.">
    <h3>Build 2: use a zero object relative</h3><p class="tile-target">Identify the projector by Omar’s test. Omit object <span class="ex">that</span>.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="room">Room</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="omar">Omar</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="projector">projector</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="three">Three</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="tested">tested</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="in">in</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the reference</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="which" data-hint="The noun engineer refers to a person in this context." data-fix="The engineer who designed the ramp is presenting today." data-why="Use who or that for a person; which refers to a thing." data-success-message="Correct. Who connects the person engineer to the subject action designed.">
    <h3>Repair 1: match the human referent</h3><p>Tap the relative word that treats the engineer as a thing.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="engineer">The engineer</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="which">which</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="designed">designed the ramp</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="today">is presenting today.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="it" data-hint="That already represents the projector as the object of tested." data-fix="The projector that Omar tested works well." data-why="Do not repeat an object with it when the relative word already carries that role." data-success-message="Correct. Removing it leaves one subject, Omar, and one represented object, the projector.">
    <h3>Repair 2: remove the repeated object</h3><p>Tap the extra object pronoun.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="projector">The projector</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="that">that</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="omar">Omar tested</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it">it</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="works">works well.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="in" data-hint="Where already carries the meaning in the room in this sentence." data-fix="This is the room where we store the tables." data-why="Use either the room where we store the tables or the room that we store the tables in, not both place relationships together." data-success-message="Correct. Removing the final in prevents a redundant place relationship.">
    <h3>Repair 3: express the place relationship once</h3><p>Tap the redundant preposition.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="room">This is the room</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="where">where</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we">we store</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="tables">the tables</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="in">in.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it without exposing private people or places</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to identify a real employer, coworker, client, family member, address, private room, accessibility need, schedule, safety record, device, organization, or personal relationship. Use Nia, Omar, Lena, the workshop, and the fictional rooms and equipment on this page. Real details are optional.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>People:</b> Choose a trainer, coordinator, and volunteer group. Give each one an essential clue using <span class="ex">who</span> or <span class="ex">whose</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Things:</b> Choose one of two projectors and one of two files. Use one subject relative and one zero object relative.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Places:</b> Identify the correct room once with <span class="ex">where</span> and once with <span class="ex">that ... in</span>. Explain why you would not combine both patterns.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Information:</b> Make every clause necessary to choose the referent. Keep it beside its noun and read it without a comma-like pause.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: present a 75–90 second fictional shortlist</h3>
    <p>Recommend one person, one organization, one thing, and one place for Nia’s workshop. The listener must choose among at least two options in each category. Use <span class="ex">who</span>, one defining <span class="ex">that</span> or <span class="ex">which</span>, <span class="ex">whose + noun</span>, and <span class="ex">where</span>. Include one subject relative that cannot be omitted, one zero object relative, and one verb whose number agrees with the noun it identifies.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener identify every exact referent, locate the subject and open role inside each clause, explain one omission, hear one continuous rhythm group, and distinguish the essential clues from optional extra information?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You kept subject who, omitted only object that, and represented the organization-volunteer relationship with whose.">
    <h3>Final check: defend the identifying structure</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the technician who repairs the projectors" data-hint="Who performs repairs, so the subject relative must remain." data-fix="Use the technician who repairs the projectors."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which phrase has a required subject relative?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the technician who repairs the projectors">the technician who repairs the projectors</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the technician Nia recommended">the technician Nia recommended</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the projector Omar tested">the projector Omar tested</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The projector the coordinator reserved is available." data-hint="The coordinator remains as subject of reserved, so object that may be omitted." data-fix="The projector the coordinator reserved is available."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence accurately uses a zero object relative?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The projector the coordinator reserved is available.">The projector the coordinator reserved is available.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The projector stopped working is unavailable.">The projector stopped working is unavailable.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The projector that the coordinator reserved it is available.">The projector that the coordinator reserved it is available.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the organization whose volunteers completed the training" data-hint="Whose must connect the organization to the associated noun volunteers." data-fix="Use the organization whose volunteers completed the training."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which phrase accurately identifies an organization through its volunteers?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the organization whose volunteers completed the training">the organization whose volunteers completed the training</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the organization who volunteers completed the training">the organization who volunteers completed the training</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the organization where volunteers it completed the training">the organization where volunteers it completed the training</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect: what exact noun does the clue identify?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">A defining clause is essential when...</span> <span class="ex">I keep the relative word when...</span> <span class="ex">I may omit it when...</span> <span class="ex">Whose is followed by...</span> <span class="ex">Where already means...</span> <span class="ex">I avoid what after a noun because...</span></p>
