  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Next-day subject-object gap, where pattern, and reference retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Return without rereading the page. Locate the noun, the subject inside the relative clause, and the role that points back to the noun before selecting an answer.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You retained the subject-object gap distinction, the single place relationship, and the no-repeated-object rule.">
      <h3>Three delayed checks</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The tutor who teaches evenings is available." data-hint="Who is the subject of teaches, so it must remain." data-fix="The tutor who teaches evenings is available."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence keeps the required subject relative?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The tutor who teaches evenings is available.">The tutor who teaches evenings is available.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The tutor teaches evenings is available.">The tutor teaches evenings is available.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The tutor who she teaches evenings is available.">The tutor who she teaches evenings is available.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Both are grammatical; where includes the place relationship, while that works with final in." data-hint="Compare where we work with that we work in; each expresses the place relationship once." data-fix="Both are grammatical; where includes the place relationship, while that works with final in."><p class="quiz-question">2. What is accurate about <span class="ex">the room where we work</span> and <span class="ex">the room that we work in</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both are grammatical; where includes the place relationship, while that works with final in.">Both are grammatical; where includes the place relationship, while that works with final in.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Only the room where we work in is grammatical.">Only the room where we work in is grammatical.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both require what after the noun room.">Both require what after the noun room.</button></div></div>
